Dear Hamad,

I hope you are well, our colleagues in Roads and Traffic passed along your =
email to us here in the Events section.
Thank you for bringing this matter to our attention.
We appreciate the significance of the upcoming Brazilian elections and the =
importance of ensuring that the Brazilian community in Dublin can access th=
e RDS and exercise their right to vote.
I have raised the matter with the Dublin Marathon Group and have made them =
aware of the concerns you have outlined regarding access on the 25th of Oct=
ober, should a second round of voting be required. I have also highlighted =
the scale of the event and the importance of facilitating access for the ap=
proximately 17,000 registered voters expected to participate.
If you are happy for me to do so, I can forward your email directly to the =
team at the Dublin Marathon Group, to ensure they have the full context and=
 details of your concerns.
Thank you again for reaching out and for outlining the steps already taken =
with An Garda S=EDoch=E1na and other stakeholders. We will pass your concer=
ns on to the relevant parties for their consideration.
Kind Regards,

Siobh=E1n Tivnan

